 "notes": "Headline new observational bound: the 'X-ray and gamma-ray limits on lifetime' curve in Fig. 2 (light-grey exclusion boundary), the paper's own derived limit on g_ae for ALP dark matter that decays radiatively (a->gamma gamma, Eqs. 2-4). This diagonal jagged curve is the boundary; couplings ABOVE it are excluded. Extracted as a vector path (drawing 17) from the e-print figure combplDM.pdf, calibrated on the axis tick labels (x: m_a in MeV log scale; y: |g_ae| log scale), then resampled at 50 log-spaced masses; the narrow upward spikes are real features of the astrophysical (NuSTAR/XMM-Newton/INTEGRAL) line-search sensitivity. Mass axis converted MeV->eV. Paper assumes the ALP is 100% of the dark matter; no single local density is quoted (galactic/M31 halo profiles used), so dm_density_assumed is null. This is a reinterpretation-type paper but derives its own bound; it supersedes the direct-detection lab limits (LUX/PandaX/XENON1T/XMASS/SuperCDMS/Majorana/EDELWEISS/GERDA) shown as coloured regions. The dark-grey 'Lifetime<13.8 Gyr' region is a separate self-consistency band, not reported. CL not restated in paper; astro limits taken at 95%.",
